---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Terms of Service, MIT License & Affiliate Disclosure | QuadletGen"
	description="Terms of use for QuadletGen: MIT license grant, operator staging verification duties for systemd units and SELinux volume labels, and VPS affiliate disclosure."
	canonicalPath="/terms/"
	showComparison={false}
>
	<article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 sm:py-14 lg:px-8">
		<header class="border-b border-slate-800 pb-8">
			<p class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-cyan-400">
				Last Updated: November 12, 2026
			</p>
			<h1 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl">
				Terms of Service and Infrastructure Disclosure
			</h1>
			<p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-300 sm:text-base">
				By accessing or using QuadletGen (<code class="text-cyan-300">quadletgen.com</code>), you agree to the operational terms, MIT open-source license conditions, and sponsorship disclosures set out below.
			</p>
		</header>

		<div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-300 sm:text-base">
			<section class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 p-6 sm:p-8">
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white sm:text-xl">
					1. MIT License grant and ownership of generated unit files
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3">
					QuadletGen's clean-room parser, Quadlet unit formatter, sample templates, and web workbench are provided under the MIT License. You retain complete ownership and unrestricted rights to copy, edit, commit to private or public repositories, automate, and deploy any <code class="text-cyan-300">.container</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300">.network</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300">.volume</code>, and <code class="text-cyan-300">.env</code> files generated in your browser for personal, academic, open-source, or commercial workloads without attribution requirements on your generated infrastructure configs.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="rounded-xl border border-amber-500/30 bg-amber-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8">
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white sm:text-xl">
					2. Operator responsibility for staging review, systemd units, and SELinux labels
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3">
					Generated Quadlet files configure operating-system services, host port bindings, container capabilities, device pass-throughs, and filesystem security labels. Automated translation from Docker Compose YAML or CLI flags is a starting aid, not a substitute for systems administration review. Before deploying generated files to any production Linux host, you are solely responsible for performing these verification checks:
				</p>
				<ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate-300">
					<li>
						<strong class="font-semibold text-white">Audit SELinux bind-mount relabeling (<code class="text-amber-200">:z</code> and <code class="text-amber-200">:Z</code>).</strong> Appending <code class="text-amber-200">:z</code> or <code class="text-amber-200">:Z</code> instructs Podman to recursively relabel the host directory's SELinux context. Never apply <code class="text-amber-200">:z</code> or <code class="text-amber-200">:Z</code> to broad host directories such as <code class="text-amber-200">/</code>, <code class="text-amber-200">/etc</code>, <code class="text-amber-200">/usr</code>, <code class="text-amber-200">/var</code>, or your top-level <code class="text-amber-200">/home/$USER</code> folder, as relabeling system paths can break <code class="text-amber-200">sshd</code> or host daemons. Always scope mounts to dedicated application subdirectories and verify in a non-production staging VM first.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong class="font-semibold text-white">Run the Podman Quadlet dry-run validator.</strong> Test generated syntax against your host's exact Podman binary with <code class="break-all text-amber-200">/usr/libexec/podman/quadlet --dryrun --user</code> (or <code class="break-all text-amber-200">/usr/libexec/podman/quadlet --dryrun</code> for rootful units) before executing <code class="text-amber-200">systemctl daemon-reload</code>.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong class="font-semibold text-white">Lock down secret files and privileged flags.</strong> Restrict extracted <code class="text-amber-200">.env</code> files with <code class="text-amber-200">chmod 600</code>, verify published host interfaces (for example binding internal ports to <code class="text-amber-200">127.0.0.1</code> behind a reverse proxy), review <code class="text-amber-200">AddCapability=</code> or <code class="text-amber-200">PodmanArgs=--privileged</code> directives, and confirm tested backups exist prior to restarting stateful databases.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 p-6 sm:p-8">
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white sm:text-xl">
					3. Disclaimer of warranties and limitation of liability
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3">
					THE SOFTWARE AND GENERATED CONFIGURATIONS ARE PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL QUADLETGEN OR ITS AUTHORS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, DATA LOSS, SERVICE OUTAGE, SELINUX RELABELING IMPACT, SECURITY INCIDENT, OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT, OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF, OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE WORKBENCH OR THE DEPLOYMENT OF GENERATED SYSTEMD UNITS.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 p-6 sm:p-8">
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white sm:text-xl">
					4. Linux VPS affiliate and sponsorship disclosure (<code class="text-cyan-300">rel="sponsored"</code>)
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3">
					QuadletGen is free to use with zero container limits, zero registration walls, and zero server uploads. To fund domain and maintenance costs, deployment guides on this site may display optional referral links to Linux cloud infrastructure providers suited for Podman 4.4+ and 5.x workloads, such as Hetzner Cloud, DigitalOcean, or Vultr.
				</p>
				<ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate-300">
					<li>
						<strong class="font-semibold text-white">Explicit link labeling.</strong> Every paid sponsorship or affiliate referral link carries <code class="text-cyan-300">rel="sponsored noopener"</code> in HTML markup and appears beside plain-language disclosure copy in accordance with FTC 16 CFR Part 255 guidelines and Google Search link spam policies.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong class="font-semibold text-white">No extra cost to you.</strong> If you sign up through a referral link, QuadletGen may receive a commission or hosting credit at zero additional cost to you (and in some partner programs, new users receive starter cloud credits).
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong class="font-semibold text-white">Deterministic converter independence.</strong> Sponsorships never alter Quadlet unit generation, SELinux mount recommendations, or technical comparisons.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 p-6 sm:p-8">
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white sm:text-xl">
					5. Acceptable use, trademarks, and contact
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3">
					You agree not to misrepresent QuadletGen as an official Red Hat, IBM, or Docker product, and not to launch automated denial-of-service traffic against <code class="text-cyan-300">quadletgen.com</code>. Podman and Red Hat are trademarks of Red Hat, Inc., and Docker is a trademark of Docker, Inc. (see our <a href="/about/" class="font-medium text-cyan-300 underline decoration-cyan-500/40 underline-offset-4 hover:text-cyan-200">About page</a>).
				</p>
				<p class="mt-3">
					Questions about these terms, open-source licensing, or affiliate disclosures can be sent to <a href="mailto:hello@quadletgen.com" class="font-mono font-medium text-cyan-300 underline decoration-cyan-500/40 underline-offset-4 hover:text-cyan-200">hello@quadletgen.com</a>. Read our <a href="/privacy/" class="font-medium text-cyan-300 underline decoration-cyan-500/40 underline-offset-4 hover:text-cyan-200">Privacy Policy</a> for data-handling guarantees.
				</p>
			</section>
		</div>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
